# FPS_Player.events — the first-person player's feel and setup (Task_FPS Phases 1–3).
#
# The keys themselves are not here: `include "FPS_Controls"` pulls in the shared controller
# (W/A/S/D, Shift sprint, Ctrl crouch, Space jump, Escape cursor lock). This file only holds
# what is specific to this player — the speed numbers, the stamina bar and the capture on
# start — so a second first-person character is a copy of these three lines plus the include.
#
# Scene setup: the player actor carries this sheet's EventSheet with
#   First Person, Use Physics Movement and Move Relative To Camera ticked,
# and a Camera actor is parented under it at eye height
# (that child is the eyes: the mouse pitches it).
#
# Feel knobs are globals: `set LookSensitivity to 0.15`, `set LookInvertY to 1`.

when game starts
  lock cursor
  # Every `move` in FPS_Controls asks for `my Pace`, so this one number is the walk speed;
  # 240 × 1.75 = 420 while sprinting.
  set my Pace to 240
  set my SprintSpeed to 1.75
  set my Stamina to 100

include "FPS_Controls"
